      "title": "Student Employment Services",
      "description": "Student Employment - SUNY Cortland Skip to main content myRedDragon Offices A-Z Visitors Guide Information for Future Students Current Students Parents/Families Faculty/Staff Alumni Community Members Submit Search Main Menu Toggle Section Menu Toggle Submit Search Information for Future Students Current Students Parents/Families Faculty/Staff Alumni Community Members About About Maps/‌Directions Facts/‌Figures Contact Us Campus Priorities Accolades Leadership History Accreditations We Are the Red Dragons Website Information Social Media Directory More + about SUNY Cortland Academics Academics Academic Calendars Academic Departments Academic Resources University Catalogs Undergraduate Academics Majors/‌Minors Pre-professional Programs Course\n                            Schedule Honors Program Study Abroad Teacher Education Summer Session Winter Session Graduate Academics Programs Assistantships Graduate Student Support Graduate Catalog More + about Academics Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Freshmen Applicants Transfer Students International Students Readmission Accepted Students Undergraduate students Apply Visit Undergraduate FAQs Enrollment Facts Get Connected with Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Admission Criteria All Programs Online/‌Hybrid Programs Assistantships Dates/‌Deadlines Graduate students Apply Graduate Catalog Graduate FAQs International Graduate Students Get Connected with Graduate Admissions More + about Admissions Tuition/‌Aid Tuition/‌Aid Student Accounts Office Tuition and Costs Billing/‌Payment Room Rates College Fees Refunds/‌Withdrawals Financial Aid Office Types of Aid Apply for Aid Financial Aid Forms Scholarships Graduate Funding More + about Tuition and Financial Aid Student Life Student Life Clubs and Organizations Campus Services Student Life Center Residence Life On-Campus Living Campus Recreation Health/‌Wellness Diversity Student Employment Off-Campus Living More + about Student Life Athletics Athletics Cortland Red Dragons Staff Directory Schedule Facilities Recruits Champions C-Club More + about Athletics Giving Giving Ways to Give Find Your Cause Naming Opportunities Give\n                            Now More + about Giving Student Employment Services Home Offices Career Services Student Employment Services What are Student Employment Services (SES)? Career Services engages with students and employers to offer a variety of opportunities both on and off campus that will serve college students’ ever-changing schedules, and provide necessary employment skills development. We also process I-9 verification and collect tax withholding information for NYS student assistants on-campus. On-Campus Job Postings SUNY Cortland Auxiliary Services (Dining and Bookstore) Off-Campus Job postings powered by Handshake Student Employment Policies and Procedures SES for Students SES for Faculty/Staff Members SES for Community Members NACE Professional Skills and Competencies: The National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) serves as a benchmark for Career Services and provides research on employers, employment trends, and best practices. NACE’s core competencies are skills employers believe college students should develop throughout their academic career. Below are four of eight important competencies to practice during a student work experience. For more information on professional competencies, contact Career Services. Communication Clearly and effectively exchange information, ideas, facts, and perspectives with persons inside and outside of an organization. Sample Behaviors: Understand the importance of and demonstrate verbal, written, and non-verbal/body language, abilities. Employ active listening, persuasion, and influencing skills. Communicate in a clear and organized manner so that others can effectively understand. Frame communication with respect to diversity of learning styles, varied individual communication abilities, and cultural differences. Ask appropriate questions for specific information from supervisors, specialists, and others. Promptly inform relevant others when needing guidance with assigned tasks. Critical Thinking Clearly and effectively exchange information, ideas, facts, and perspectives with persons inside and outside of an organization. Sample Behaviors: Make decisions and solve problems using sound, inclusive reasoning and judgment. Gather and analyze information from a diverse set of sources and individuals to fully understand a problem. Proactively anticipate needs and prioritize action steps. Accurately summarize and interpret data with an awareness of personal biases that may impact outcomes. Effectively communicate actions and rationale, recognizing the diverse perspectives and lived experiences of stakeholders. Multi-task well in a fast-paced environment. Professionalism Knowing work environments differ greatly, understand and demonstrate effective work habits, and act in the interest of the larger community and workplace. Sample Behaviors: Act equitably with integrity and accountability to self, others, and the organization. Maintain a positive personal brand in alignment with organization and personal career values. Be present and prepared. Demonstrate dependability (e.g., report consistently for work or meetings). Prioritize and complete tasks to accomplish organizational goals. Consistently meet or exceed goals and expectations. Have an attention to detail, resulting in few if any errors in their work. Show a high level of dedication toward doing a good job. Teamwork Build and maintain collaborative relationships to work effectively toward common goals, while appreciating diverse viewpoints and shared responsibilities. Sample Behaviors: Listen carefully to others, taking time to understand and ask appropriate questions without interrupting. Effectively manage conflict, interact with and respect diverse personalities, and meet ambiguity with resilience. Be accountable for individual and team responsibilities and deliverables. Employ personal strengths, knowledge, and talents to complement those of others. Exercise the ability to compromise and be agile. Collaborate with others to achieve common goals. Build strong, positive working relationships with supervisor and team members/coworkers. Contact Us Visit Student Employment Services in Career Services, Van Hoesen Hall, Room B-5 Student Employment Services: 607-753-2223, Email SES Student Employment Coordinator: 607-753-4715, Alexis Shura Student Employment Recognition Yearbook Student employees perform invaluable service to campus with enthusiasm, dedication, and initiative. To celebrate their contributions to the SUNY Cortland community, Career Services would like to present the 2025-2026 Student Employee Appreciation Yearbook featuring 49 student employee honorees and numerous student spotlights from students who volunteered to share something from their part-time employment experience . This project was initiated in Spring 2020 as an ongoing, annual, digital yearbook series for Student Employee Recognition. Thank you, students for all you do! 2024-2025 Student Employee Appreciation Yearbook 2023-2024 Student Employee Appreciation Yearbook 2022-2023 Student Employee Appreciation Yearbook Toggle page navigation Menu Career Services Handshake Handshake Login Events Career Design Resources Career Readiness Having Career Conversations Graduate School Resumes and Cover Letters Personal Brand Interview Essentials Equity and Inclusion Resources Focus 2 Student Employment Services SES for Students SES for Faculty/Staff SES for Community Internships Creating or Finding Your Own Opportunities Internship and Living Stipends Internship Guide Micro-Internships Teacher Certification Teacher Certification Overview First Destinations Employers/Recruiters Staff, Mission, and Values Contact us Career Services Van Hoesen Hall, Room B-5 Phone: 607-753-2223 Fax: 607-753-2937 Email SES Visit Apply Request