 + about Student Life Athletics Athletics Cortland Red Dragons Staff Directory Schedule Facilities Recruits Champions C-Club More + about Athletics Giving Giving Ways to Give Find Your Cause Naming Opportunities Give\n                            Now More + about Giving Work for us! Home Offices The Learning Center Student Employment Would You Like to Work for The Learning Center? “I have enjoyed my time working as a peer tutor. I wish I had started sooner.” \"Being a supplemental instruction leader has been such a rewarding experience that has allowed me to help my peers better understand challenging topics. I love watching them succeed and seeing all their hard work pay off. I think the work we do is so valuable not only for the students who attend sessions but also for myself as someone in the major; it gives me a better understanding of material that I can also apply in my own classes. I think being a SI leader has made me a better overall student and even gives me an edge up when applying for jobs related to my future career goals.\" We regularly hire students for the following positions: Peer Tutor Supplemental Instruction Leader Student Assistant - Receptionist (directly and through work-study) Visit SUNY Cortland's Campus Employment Website. Information about Graduate Assistantships is available through Graduate Admissions. Toggle page navigation Menu The Learning Center The Learning Center Staff About Us Tutoring/Academic Support Professional Tutoring Professional Tutoring Overview Walk-In Tutoring Walk-In Tutoring Nightowl Online Tutoring Peer Tutoring Peer Tutoring Overview Supplemental Instruction Supplemental Instruction Overview Student Resources Student Resources Academic Success Checklist Active Reading Tips Challenging Text Tips Cornell Note-taking Learning from Home Learning Space Note-Taking Tips Preparing for Finals A Strategy for Learning Math Time Management Tech Tips Student Employment For Faculty / Staff TLC Referral Form STAR-NY Visit Apply Request Info Employment Off-Campus Locations Campus Store Library Maps/​Directions Admissions Visits Virtual Tour Consumer Information Campus Safety Web Accessibility (opens new window) Complete the general Contact Us form PO Box 2000 Cortland, NY 13045 607-753-2011 FOLLOW US Cookie Consent We use cookies and similar technologies to improve your website experience and help us understand how you navigate our website. By using this site, you agree to our Privacy Policy . I Agree"
    },
