    "https://www2.cortland.edu/offices/hr/benefits/": {
      "title": "Benefits",
      "description": "Benefits - SUNY Cortland Skip to main content myRedDragon Offices A-Z Visitors Guide Information for Future Students Current Students Parents/Families Faculty/Staff Alumni Community Members Submit Search Main Menu Toggle Section Menu Toggle Submit Search Information for Future Students Current Students Parents/Families Faculty/Staff Alumni Community Members About About Maps/‌Directions Facts/‌Figures Contact Us Campus Priorities Accolades Leadership History Accreditations We Are the Red Dragons Website Information Social Media Directory More + about SUNY Cortland Academics Academics Academic Calendars Academic Departments Academic Resources University Catalogs Undergraduate Academics Majors/‌Minors Pre-professional Programs Course\n                            Schedule Honors Program Study Abroad Teacher Education Summer Session Winter Session Graduate Academics Programs Assistantships Graduate Student Support Graduate Catalog More + about Academics Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Freshmen Applicants Transfer Students International Students Readmission Accepted Students Undergraduate students Apply Visit Undergraduate FAQs Enrollment Facts Get Connected with Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Admission Criteria All Programs Online/‌Hybrid Programs Assistantships Dates/‌Deadlines Graduate students Apply Graduate Catalog Graduate FAQs International Graduate Students Get Connected with Graduate Admissions More + about Admissions Tuition/‌Aid Tuition/‌Aid Student Accounts Office Tuition and Costs Billing/‌Payment Room Rates College Fees Refunds/‌Withdrawals Financial Aid Office Types of Aid Apply for Aid Financial Aid Forms Scholarships Graduate Funding More + about Tuition and Financial Aid Student Life Student Life Clubs and Organizations Campus Services Student Life Center Residence Life On-Campus Living Campus Recreation Health/‌Wellness Diversity Student Employment Off-Campus Living More + about Student Life Athletics Athletics Cortland Red Dragons Staff Directory Schedule Facilities Recruits Champions C-Club More + about Athletics Giving Giving Ways to Give Find Your Cause Naming Opportunities Give\n                            Now More + about Giving Benefits Home Offices Human Resources Benefits We are pleased to present a summary of employee benefits website. As New York State employees, we enjoy a wide array of benefits, and understanding these benefits is not always easy. Benefits change rapidly and we will attempt to keep this website as up to date as possible. SUNY has developed a terrific website on SUNY Benefits . We encourage you to bookmark this site as it has extremely valuable and helpful information. It includes many downloadable forms, detailed information about the various benefits programs, and links to additional resources. It also contains a separate section on benefit information for prospective employees. This site will be continuously updated as changes to benefits are made. Benefit Summaries CSEA Employees Full-Time UUP Employees Part-Time UUP Employees Management/Confidential Employees NYSCOPBA Employees PBANYS Employees PEF Employees Graduate Student Employees Union Paid Family Leave As of January 1, 2019, PFL is available to unclassified Management/Confidential (SUNY MC13) and UUP-represented employees, and may become available to other union-represented employees through the collective bargaining process. This webpage discusses PFL program details for unclassified Management/Confidential (SUNY MC13) and UUP-represented employees. View the PFL Policy for UUP-represented employees. View the PFL program available to classified groups (e.g., MC06 employees). The purpose of PFL is to help employees with work-life balance by providing a paid leave alternative to charging paid leave accruals for leaves of absence to attend to family* needs associated with: the birth or placement of a biological, adopted, or foster child (first 12 months) a family member's serious health condition (physical or psychological care) a call to active duty in the U.S. armed forces (qualifying exigency) Retirement Phased Retirement Application Phased Retirement Assignment/Work Schedule Phased Retirement Policy Retirement Privileges Policy Important Links CSEA Benefits New York State Health & Prescription Insurance PEF (Public Employees Federation, AFL-CIO) Benefits SUNY Statewide Benefits (General information for all State Benefits) UUP Benefits Toggle page navigation Menu Benefits Employee Education Benefits Provider Contact Information Benefits Orientation Benefits Orientation CSEA Benefits Orientation UUP Benefits Orientation Contact Us Miller Building, Room 302 Phone: 607-753-2302 Fax: 607-753-5994 Email Hours: 8 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Benefits Administrator Visit Apply Request Info Employment Off-Campus Locations Campus Store Library Maps/​Directions Admissions Visits Virtual Tour Consumer Information Campus Safety Web Accessibility (opens new window) Complete the general Contact Us form PO Box 2000 Cortland, NY 13045 607-753-2011 FOLLOW US Cookie Consent We use cookies and similar technologies to improve your website experience and help us understand how you navigate our website. By using this site, you agree to our Privacy Policy . I Agree"
    },
    "https://www2.cortland.edu/offices/hr/jobs": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Employment Opportunities - SUNY Cortland Skip to main content myRedDragon Offices A-Z Visitors Guide Information for Future Students Current Students Parents/Families Faculty/Staff Alumni Community Members Submit Search Main Menu Toggle Section Menu Toggle Submit Search Information for Future Students Current Students Parents/Families Faculty/Staff Alumni Community Members About About Maps/‌Directions Facts/‌Figures Contact Us Campus Priorities Accolades Leadership History Accreditations We Are the Red Dragons Website Information Social Media Directory More + about SUNY Cortland Academics Academics Academic Calendars Academic Departments Academic Resources University Catalogs Undergraduate Academics Majors/‌Minors Pre-professional Programs Course\n                            Schedule Honors Program Study Abroad Teacher Education Summer Session Winter Session Graduate Academics Programs Assistantships Graduate Student Support Graduate Catalog More + about Academics Admissions Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Freshmen Applicants Transfer Students International Students Readmission Accepted Students Undergraduate students Apply Visit Undergraduate FAQs Enrollment Facts Get Connected with Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Admission Criteria All Programs Online/‌Hybrid Programs Assistantships Dates/‌Deadlines Graduate students Apply Graduate Catalog Graduate FAQs International Graduate Students Get Connected with Graduate Admissions More + about Admissions Tuition/‌Aid Tuition/‌Aid Student Accounts Office Tuition and Costs Billing/‌Payment Room Rates College Fees Refunds/‌Withdrawals Financial Aid Office Types of Aid Apply for Aid Financial Aid Forms Scholarships Graduate Funding More + about Tuition and Financial Aid Student Life Student Life Clubs and Organizations Campus Services Student Life Center Residence Life On-Campus Living Campus Recreation Health/‌Wellness Diversity Student Employment Off-Campus Living More + about Student Life Athletics Athletics Cortland Red Dragons Staff Directory Schedule Facilities Recruits Champions C-Club More + about Athletics Giving Giving Ways to Give Find Your Cause Naming Opportunities Give\n                            Now More + about Giving Employment Opportunities Home Offices Human Resources Jobs For the past 150 years, SUNY Cortland has been dedicated to creating a workplace environment that focuses on diversity, equity, and inclusion. The college is committed to eliminating the systemic and historical barriers of discrimination in order to provide equal opportunity and education for all. SUNY Cortland uses an online employment system that allows applicants to create a unique account and apply online for positions with the College. This account also allows you access to view the status of your application(s). Our vacancy page can be visited directly at jobs.cortland.edu . Please note that you must have a Javascript-enabled web browser to use the site. If you are unable to read or otherwise view or access our employment site please contact our office at 607-753-2302 for assistance. View SUNY Cortland Job Postings Please carefully review the posting details (Special Instructions for Applying section) to determine the application needs of the position you are seeking. General Information New York State Department of Civil Service New York State Examinations Canvass Applicants Department of Civil Service (Eligible List Management System) Cortland Auxiliary Services Cortland Auxiliary is a private, not-for-profit organization that provides the SUNY Cortland community with food services and the Campus Store. Cortland Auxiliary vacancy announcements Undergraduate/Graduate Student Employment Student Employment Services Cortland Auxiliary vacancy announcements Graduate Assistantships (GA's) The Learning Center positions Orientation Assistant Quick Links About working at SUNY Cortland SUNY Job Benefits SUNY Cortland Job application portal Live in Cortland SUNY Cortland's Mission and Vision Thank you for your interest in SUNY Cortland. Toggle page navigation Menu Human Resources Benefits Benefits Employee Education Benefits Provider Contact Information Benefits Orientation Benefits Orientation CSEA Benefits Orientation UUP Benefits Orientation Forms Hire Right Recruitment Workshops Human Resources Staff Organizational Chart Who do I Contact for Assistance? Staff Jobs Live in Cortland Policies and Procedures Training and Development Unions Welcome To NYS Employment Visit Apply Request Info Employment Off-Campus Locations Campus Store Library Maps/​Directions Admissions Visits Virtual Tour Consumer Information Campus Safety Web Accessibility (opens new window) Complete the general Contact Us form PO Box 2000 Cortland, NY 13045 607-753-2011 FOLLOW US Cookie Consent We use cookies and similar technologies to improve your website experience and help us understand how you navigate our website. By using this site, you agree to our Privacy Policy . I Agree"
    }
